refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
arrayfalsegrapheme_str_split stringstring intlength1
This function will return an array of strings, it is a version of str_split with support for grapheme cluster byte characters. If the length parameter is specified, the string is broken down into chunks of the specified length in grapheme clusters (not bytes).

&reftitle.returnvalues;
grapheme_str_split returns an array of strings, &return.falseforfailure;.
If string is the empty string, an empty array is returned.

&reftitle.examples;
grapheme_str_split example
A grapheme cluster made of several code points is kept together, where str_split and mb_str_split would break it apart.
<?php var_dump(grapheme_str_split("a\u{1F469}\u{200D}\u{1F469}\u{200D}\u{1F467}b")); ?>
&example.outputs;
array(3) { [0]=> string(1) "a" [1]=> string(18) "👩‍👩‍👧" [2]=> string(1) "b" }

&reftitle.seealso;
str_split mb_str_split
Unicode Text Segmentation: Grapheme Cluster Boundaries
